# repo-forensics suppressions. Syntax: rule:<rule-id>[:<path-glob>]
# Reviewed and verified benign 2026-08-11. These are the highest-volume rule classes that match
# ordinary shell idioms in this repo (a CLI whose job is orchestrating other CLIs) rather than
# real issues. Genuinely security-relevant rules (eval, injection, dataflow, workflow triggers)
# are deliberately LEFT VISIBLE so real findings in those classes still surface.

# SA-SH-004  Nested Command Substitution — 100% `$(( $(date +%s) - t0 ))` / `"$(cd "$(dirname "$0")")"`
#            idioms; a pure-syntax detector with ~0 true-positive value on shell. No tainted input.
rule:SA-SH-004

# ST-ST-003  Stderr suppression + background exec — `... 2>/dev/null && ...` fallbacks and the
#            product's OWN supervised-background delegation (jobs are logged to $OSRC_HOME/jobs/*).
rule:ST-ST-003

# ST-ST-004  Full output suppression + background — same supervised-bg nature; the one sh -c site
#            (OSRC_HEARTBEAT_WAKE) takes untrusted text only via $1/stdin/env, never the command
#            string, and sanitizes control chars (traced in the code's own comment).
rule:ST-ST-004

# SC-NET-001 Hardcoded IP — every hit is loopback (127.0.0.1 / ::1). Loopback-only binding IS the
#            security control; the translation shim now also validates its upstream is loopback.
rule:SC-NET-001

# SC-SEC-007 Fake API-key fixtures — clearly-fake, non-rotatable values that EXIST to exercise the
#            repo's own secret-scan / cloud-gate / redaction. Scoped to the test files only.
rule:SC-SEC-007:plugins/outsourcerer/skills/outsourcerer/scripts/tests

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEFT VISIBLE (NOT suppressed) and accepted-with-reason — real findings in these classes must stay
# surfaced, so we do NOT spend a suppression slot on them:
#   * SA-SH-001 eval — trap -p save/restore + tests eval-ing the repo's OWN source; individually
#     audited. A future eval of untrusted data SHOULD still flag, so this stays visible.
#   * dataflow / exfiltration (shim) — operator-set config -> localhost proxy; now loopback-guarded.
#   * ci-cd (GHA pull_request_target in cla.yml) — correctly built: workflow-level permissions:{},
#     SHA-pinned action, and NO checkout of PR head code. Invariant, accepted.
#   * ST-PI-005 / ST-MH-003 — prose/comments in CHANGELOG/README/mechanism matched as "directives".
#   * SA-SH-004-adjacent: the tap `sh -c "$orig"` is now perms-guarded (0600 + world-writable refuse).
